1
00:00:07,220 --> 00:00:13,640
A phone plan costs 12 dollars a month, plus 10 cents for every text you send.

2
00:00:13,690 --> 00:00:16,540
This month you send 50 texts.

3
00:00:16,590 --> 00:00:17,950
How much is the bill?

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,500
Pause the video and work it out.

5
00:00:21,550 --> 00:00:25,120
50 texts at 10 cents each cost 5 dollars.

6
00:00:25,170 --> 00:00:26,800
Add the 12 dollars.

7
00:00:26,850 --> 00:00:29,380
The bill is 17 dollars.

8
00:00:29,430 --> 00:00:33,170
We can write one rule that works for any number of texts.

9
00:00:33,220 --> 00:00:36,580
Call the number of texts t, and the cost C.

10
00:00:36,630 --> 00:00:38,870
C equals 12 plus 0.1 times t.

11
00:00:38,920 --> 00:00:42,340
A rule like this is called a formula.

12
00:00:42,390 --> 00:00:45,260
Remember: 3 n means 3 times n.

13
00:00:45,310 --> 00:00:49,920
In 2 a plus 5, you multiply a by 2 first, then add 5.

14
00:00:49,970 --> 00:00:55,960
To substitute means to replace a letter with a number, and then work out the value.

15
00:00:56,010 --> 00:00:58,470
Take 3 a plus 2, when a is 4.

16
00:00:58,520 --> 00:01:01,580
Replace a with 4: 3 times 4, plus 2.

17
00:01:01,630 --> 00:01:03,080
That is 14.

18
00:01:03,130 --> 00:01:07,410
a squared, when a is 4, is 4 times 4, which is 16.

19
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:10,040
When a is 10, it is 100.

20
00:01:10,090 --> 00:01:11,810
5, bracket, a minus 1.

21
00:01:11,860 --> 00:01:13,490
Do the bracket first.

22
00:01:13,540 --> 00:01:17,570
When a is 4, that is 5 times 3, which is 15.

23
00:01:17,620 --> 00:01:18,300
Your turn.

24
00:01:18,350 --> 00:01:21,360
Find the value of 2 a plus 7, when a is 9.

25
00:01:21,410 --> 00:01:24,730
Pause the video and try it.

26
00:01:24,780 --> 00:01:26,450
Replace a with 9.

27
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:28,070
2 times 9 is 18.

28
00:01:28,120 --> 00:01:30,240
18 plus 7 is 25.

29
00:01:30,290 --> 00:01:33,840
A formula is a rule that links two or more quantities.

30
00:01:33,890 --> 00:01:38,990
It has an equals sign, and one letter on its own, called the subject.

31
00:01:39,040 --> 00:01:42,220
You can write a formula in words, or in letters.

32
00:01:42,270 --> 00:01:45,320
Letters are shorter and easier to use.

33
00:01:45,370 --> 00:01:49,350
For 200 texts, substitute t equals 200.

34
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:52,140
C is 12 plus 0.1 times 200.

35
00:01:52,190 --> 00:01:56,210
That is 12 plus 20, so 32 dollars.

36
00:01:56,260 --> 00:01:57,550
Here is the method.

37
00:01:57,600 --> 00:02:03,460
Step 1: write the expression again, with each letter replaced by its number.

38
00:02:03,510 --> 00:02:07,070
Step 2: put in the times signs that were hidden.

39
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:09,280
3 a becomes 3 times a.

40
00:02:09,330 --> 00:02:16,840
Step 3: work it out in the right order: brackets, powers, multiply and divide, then add and subtract.

41
00:02:16,890 --> 00:02:20,320
Step 4: write the units, if there are any.

42
00:02:20,370 --> 00:02:25,010
Find the value of 3 x plus 2 y, when x is 5 and y is 4.

43
00:02:25,060 --> 00:02:26,720
Replace each letter.

44
00:02:26,770 --> 00:02:29,480
3 times 5, plus 2 times 4.

45
00:02:29,530 --> 00:02:30,830
Multiply first.

46
00:02:30,880 --> 00:02:32,290
15 plus 8.

47
00:02:32,340 --> 00:02:34,680
The answer is 23.

48
00:02:34,730 --> 00:02:36,410
Be careful with squares.

49
00:02:36,460 --> 00:02:39,110
Find 2 m squared, when m is 3.

50
00:02:39,160 --> 00:02:40,980
Only the m is squared.

51
00:02:41,030 --> 00:02:44,590
3 squared is 9, and 2 times 9 is 18.

52
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:47,370
Now find, bracket, 2 m, all squared.

53
00:02:47,420 --> 00:02:50,000
This time the bracket comes first.

54
00:02:50,050 --> 00:02:53,330
2 times 3 is 6, and 6 squared is 36.

55
00:02:53,380 --> 00:02:54,040
Your turn.

56
00:02:54,090 --> 00:02:56,980
Find x y minus 5, when x is 3 and y is 7.

57
00:02:57,030 --> 00:02:59,950
Pause and work it out.

58
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:01,920
x y means x times y.

59
00:03:01,970 --> 00:03:03,490
3 times 7 is 21.

60
00:03:03,540 --> 00:03:05,720
21 minus 5 is 16.

61
00:03:05,770 --> 00:03:11,310
Tickets cost 9 dollars each, and there is a 3 dollar booking fee for each order.

62
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:15,490
Write a formula for the total cost, T, of n tickets.

63
00:03:15,540 --> 00:03:16,970
n tickets cost 9 n.

64
00:03:17,020 --> 00:03:17,900
Add the fee.

65
00:03:17,950 --> 00:03:20,000
T equals 9 n plus 3.

66
00:03:20,050 --> 00:03:23,410
For 6 tickets, T is 9 times 6, plus 3.

67
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:26,920
That is 54 plus 3, so 57 dollars.

68
00:03:26,970 --> 00:03:30,840
Find 10 minus 2 k, when k is negative 4.

69
00:03:30,890 --> 00:03:33,730
Put the negative number in brackets.

70
00:03:33,780 --> 00:03:36,530
10 minus 2 times negative 4.

71
00:03:36,580 --> 00:03:39,390
2 times negative 4 is negative 8.

72
00:03:39,440 --> 00:03:42,620
So we have 10 minus negative 8.

73
00:03:42,670 --> 00:03:46,430
Subtracting negative 8 is the same as adding 8.

74
00:03:46,480 --> 00:03:48,350
The answer is 18.

75
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:51,010
Maya finds 3 p squared, when p is 4.

76
00:03:51,060 --> 00:03:53,620
Which line goes wrong first?

77
00:03:53,670 --> 00:03:54,770
Line 1 is wrong.

78
00:03:54,820 --> 00:03:58,670
The square belongs only to the p, not to the 3.

79
00:03:58,720 --> 00:04:00,120
Square p first.

80
00:04:00,170 --> 00:04:04,330
4 squared is 16, and 3 times 16 is 48.

81
00:04:04,380 --> 00:04:06,050
Formulas are everywhere.

82
00:04:06,100 --> 00:04:13,850
Most countries measure temperature in degrees Celsius, but the United States uses degrees Fahrenheit.

83
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:16,870
This formula changes one into the other.

84
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:19,680
F equals 1.8 times C, plus 32.

85
00:04:19,730 --> 00:04:25,940
A hot day of 30 degrees Celsius: 1.8 times 30 is 54, plus 32 is 86.

86
00:04:25,990 --> 00:04:30,880
So 30 degrees Celsius is 86 degrees Fahrenheit.

87
00:04:30,930 --> 00:04:32,170
One last question.

88
00:04:32,220 --> 00:04:37,240
Use the formula v equals u plus 10 t, to find v when u is 4 and t is 3.

89
00:04:37,290 --> 00:04:40,570
Pause the video and answer.

90
00:04:40,620 --> 00:04:41,580
Substitute.

91
00:04:41,630 --> 00:04:44,140
v equals 4, plus 10 times 3.

92
00:04:44,190 --> 00:04:47,440
That is 4 plus 30, so v is 34.

93
00:04:47,490 --> 00:04:56,310
To remember: to substitute, replace each letter by its number, put in the times signs, and follow the order of operations.

94
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:59,980
A formula links quantities, and has a subject.

95
00:05:00,030 --> 00:05:02,870
2 m squared squares only the m.

96
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:08,440
To derive a formula, say the rule in words first, then write it in letters.

97
00:05:08,490 --> 00:05:13,590
Great work! Now practise lesson 2.2 on Camday.
